{"name":"Indonesian Rattan","hex":"#d1b272","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rattan","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several species of climbing palm of the genus Calamus.","The plant used as a material for making furniture, baskets etc."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To beat with a rattan cane."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rattan"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rattan","blocks":[{"text":"Rattan, also spelled ratan, is the name for roughly 600 species of Old World climbing palms belonging to subfamily Calamoideae. The greatest diversity of rattan palm species and genera are in the closed-canopy old-growth tropical forests of Southeast Asia, though they can also be found in other parts of tropical Asia and Africa. Most rattan palms are ecologically considered lianas due to their climbing habits, unlike other palm species. A few species also have tree-like or shrub-like habits."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Thatiyan_Cuural_%28Malayalam-_%E0%B4%A4%E0%B4%9F%E0%B4%BF%E0%B4%AF%E0%B4%A8%E0%B5%8D%E2%80%8D_%E0%B4%9A%E0%B5%82%E0%B4%B0%E0%B4%B2%E0%B5%8D%E2%80%8D%29_%285661614812%29.jpg/330px-Thatiyan_Cuural_%28Malayalam-_%E0%B4%A4%E0%B4%9F%E0%B4%BF%E0%B4%AF%E0%B4%A8%E0%B5%8D%E2%80%8D_%E0%B4%9A%E0%B5%82%E0%B4%B0%E0%B4%B2%E0%B5%8D%E2%80%8D%29_%285661614812%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rattan","wikidata":"Q323021"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Daemonorops_mollis_%28rattan_palm%29_-_Bukidnon_Philippines.jpg/500px-Daemonorops_mollis_%28rattan_palm%29_-_Bukidnon_Philippines.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Daemonorops_mollis_%28rattan_palm%29_-_Bukidnon_Philippines.jpg/1280px-Daemonorops_mollis_%28rattan_palm%29_-_Bukidnon_Philippines.jpg?utm_source=en